"""Shared output identity contract for H3 generation, revision and repair."""


H3_SUBJECT_IDENTITY_POLICY = """Narrative Names are interpretation aliases for human-authored Story, Main Prompt, continuity and dialogue attribution, not final H3 identity vocabulary or binding keys. Resolve supplied names through the bounded current Narrative Name -> <Subject N> mapping without changing saved authoring fields.
For every participating mapped Subject, the exact <Subject N> token is the required canonical technical identity in final H3 prose. Translate/canonicalize human Narrative Names into their mapped <Subject N> tokens when writing structural character/entity references in summary, retention_analysis, shots/actions, camera direction, speaker attribution and sound sections. Names must not replace Subject tokens in shots. Once a Subject is defined, all subsequent structural references to that Subject must use its exact <Subject N> token.
Only in an existing valid subject_definitions entry, the CURRENT Narrative Name may appear once as natural definition prose after 'is'. Keep the existing '<Subject N> is ...' syntax and Picture provenance. This is optional orientation, not a new H3 field; if the mode has no suitable Subject-definition location, omit the name entirely from structural output. Never add a definition section unsupported by the official mode grammar. Never include retained aliases in definitions or expose them as final H3 vocabulary. Unnamed Subjects use their existing technical labels without invented name placeholders. Subject and Picture labels are distinct and never interchangeable.
Exact dialogue and lyrics remain verbatim inside <d>[Language] ...</d>. Names spoken or sung inside that literal payload are allowed and must never be substituted. Human Name: speaker labels are input attribution, not audible words; use the mapped <Subject N> for structural attribution alongside the official global speaker ID. Preserve literal visible scene text as well.
Apply this same technical identity contract to generated output, selective H3 revisions and narrow format repair. A revision must not regress a Subject token to a name. When repairing name-based structural references, restore the mapped <Subject N> while preserving action/camera meaning and exact dialogue/lyrics; never introduce new Subjects. Do not blindly substitute names across the whole prompt. Story Planner continues using current Narrative Names; Character Profiles remain Story Planner context, not direct H3 Character Profile prose."""
